{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "userdb-hotelling-multiyear-day-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.66, step 7f. `userdb-hotelling-multiyear-day`: `userdb-hotelling-multiyear` (a DEFAULT-domain run at 2015 and 2020 whose USER input database states the idle and hotelling adjustment tables) at all 24 hours under `<aggregateBy key=\"24-Hour Day\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Month\"/>`. MOVESOutput is 3,904 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is AdjustHotelling.sql's pooled table under PreAggDAY.sql: TAG adjusts 2020 over a hotellingHours table that still holds 2015's adjusted rows, here one per day type at the collapsed hour 0 (PLAN.md §7.3.61, §7.3.66).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 1952, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "time-aggregation",
      "starts",
      "output-time-step",
      "idle-adjustment",
      "multi-year"
    ]
  },
